---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PRIVACY_CHOICES_LABEL, WEBSITE_PRIVACY_HREF } from '@data/privacy';

// Set on the day this page goes live, together with the banner texts.
const LAST_UPDATED = 'November 23, 2026';

const title = 'Cookie Policy: How the Website Uses Cookies';
const description =
	'How the TBMQ website uses cookies and similar technologies: which cookies are set, what each one is for, and how you can manage or withdraw your consent.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} breadcrumb="Cookie Policy">
	<div class="cookie-policy-page">
		<div class="cookie-policy-content">
			<h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
			<p class="updated">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

			<p>
				Cookies and Local Storage are activated and used during your browsing on this site. Cookies are small text
				files, usually numbers and letters, that do not create a security risk for your computer, tablet, or smartphone.
				Local Storage is a similar mechanism used to store data, such as UTM tags, directly in your browser.
			</p>
			<p>
				This Cookie Policy explains which cookies and similar technologies we use on tbmq.io, why, and how you can
				control them. How we handle the personal data collected through them is described in our
				<a href={WEBSITE_PRIVACY_HREF}>Privacy Policy</a>.
			</p>

			<p>Cookies allow us to:</p>

			<ul>
				<li>
					Understand the behavior of visitors, measure the number of visits and page views using <a
						href="https://analytics.google.com/">Google Analytics</a
					>;
				</li>
				<li>
					Remember the campaign parameters (UTM tags) or the partner reference (<a href="https://firstpromoter.com/"
						>FirstPromoter</a
					>) stored in your browser's Local Storage when you arrive from one of our campaigns or partner links; we pass
					these parameters on to the ThingsBoard License Portal and our CRM together with your registration or contact
					request, so we know which campaign or partner it came from;
				</li>
				<li>
					Measure which of our campaigns bring contact requests: when you send us a form, Google Analytics receives the
					email address you entered, in hashed form. This happens only if you allow Marketing cookies, and no cookie is
					set for it. For this, Google Analytics also loads if you allow Marketing but not Analytics cookies; it then
					sets no cookies and sends Google only cookieless measurement data;
				</li>
				<li>
					Improve load-balancing and page load speed using <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>;
				</li>
				<li>
					Search the site using <a href="https://programmablesearchengine.google.com/"
						>Google Programmable Search Engine</a
					>. It loads only after you allow External media in the cookie banner or press "Load Google search" in the site
					search; Google then sets its own cookies, including the NID advertising cookie, and may show ads in the
					results.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				Only strictly necessary cookies are set by default. Analytics, marketing and external-media cookies are set only
				after you allow them in the cookie banner, and you can change your choice at any time via
				<button type="button" class="cookie-settings" data-cc="show-preferences">{PRIVACY_CHOICES_LABEL}</button>
				in the site footer, or delete cookies in your browser settings as described below.
			</p>
			<p>
				Your choice is stored for 180 days in the tb_consent cookie, together with the time you made it; after that, or
				if you clear your cookies, the banner is shown again. Until you allow a category, the tools in that category are
				not loaded at all: no script runs, no cookie is set and nothing is sent to the provider. The only exception is
				Google Analytics, which also loads, without setting cookies, when you allow Marketing alone (see above). If you
				reject a category or withdraw your consent later, the cookies and browser storage of that category on tbmq.io
				are deleted at once; cookies set by Google on its own domains can only be removed in your browser settings or
				your Google account. If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a refusal of
				Marketing cookies.
			</p>
			<p>
				You may also configure your browser to alert you each time cookies are created. It is also possible to prevent
				their installation or delete cookies already set. Here is the procedure to follow on the three main browsers:
			</p>

			<ul>
				<li>
					Chrome <a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647?hl=en&co=GENIE.Platform%3DDesktop"
						>instructions</a
					>;
				</li>
				<li>
					Firefox <a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox">instructions</a>;
				</li>
				<li>
					Safari <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac">instructions</a>.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<p>
				You can also opt out of Google Analytics on all websites with the <a
					href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a
				>.
			</p>

			<p>Access to our site will not be denied if you disable cookies, but some features may not work.</p>

			<h3>Cookies and similar technologies we use</h3>
			<p>
				One row per provider. Each provider's own list is linked for cookies it may set on its own domain, which we do
				not control.
			</p>

			<div class="cookie-table-wrap">
				<table class="cookie-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th>Provider</th>
							<th>Category</th>
							<th>What it stores and why</th>
							<th>Name(s)</th>
							<th>Duration</th>
							<th>More</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>TBMQ (ThingsBoard)</td>
							<td>Strictly necessary</td>
							<td>
								Your choice in the cookie banner and, in Local Storage, the color theme you picked. In Session Storage,
								for the current tab only: the state of the documentation sidebar, that you already sent feedback on a
								documentation page, that you have interacted with the site (so the GitHub star count in the header loads
								without waiting), and that star count, so it is fetched from GitHub once per visit.
							</td>
							<td>
								tb_consent; starlight-theme (Local Storage); sl-sidebar-state, feedback-submitted:&lt;page&gt;,
								tb:user-engaged, gh_stars_&lt;repository&gt; (Session Storage)
							</td>
							<td>180 days; until you clear your browser data; Session Storage until you close the tab</td>
							<td>-</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Google Analytics</td>
							<td>Analytics</td>
							<td>
								Distinguishes visitors and keeps the state of a visit, so we can count visits and page views. If you
								allowed Analytics cookies, our contact form also sends the Google Analytics client ID with your message,
								so that we can connect your request with how you found us.
							</td>
							<td>_ga; _ga_2H1PYS19HL</td>
							<td>Up to 2 years (browsers may cap it at 400 days)</td>
							<td>
								<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies">Google's cookie page</a>; <a
									href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out add-on</a
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Google Analytics (user-provided data)</td>
							<td>Marketing</td>
							<td>
								When you send us a form, the email address you entered, in hashed form, so we can measure which
								campaigns bring requests. We do not use it to build advertising profiles.
							</td>
							<td>No cookie</td>
							<td>-</td>
							<td>
								<a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/14077171">About user-provided data collection</a>
							</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>TBMQ (campaign and partner parameters)</td>
							<td>Marketing</td>
							<td>
								The UTM parameters of the campaign link, or the partner reference of the FirstPromoter affiliate link,
								you arrived from, kept in Local Storage so a later contact or registration can be attributed to that
								campaign or partner.
							</td>
							<td
								>utm (one entry with utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign, utm_term, utm_content); fpr (Local Storage)</td
							>
							<td
								>Until you withdraw your Marketing consent, it expires after 180 days, or you clear your browser data</td
							>
							<td>-</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Google Programmable Search (site search)</td>
							<td>External media</td>
							<td>
								Nothing is loaded until you allow External media or press "Load Google search" in the site search. Then,
								as soon as you open the search, Google's search script and its advertising script load; what you type is
								sent to Google as you type, to suggest queries; when you search, Google sets cookies on google.com for
								search preferences and advertising, and its search code sets one advertising cookie on tbmq.io, which we
								delete if you withdraw External media.
							</td>
							<td>NID; SEARCH_SAMESITE; __Secure-STRP (google.com); __gsas (tbmq.io)</td>
							<td>6 months; __gsas 13 months</td>
							<td><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies">Google's cookie page</a></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Cloudflare</td>
							<td>Strictly necessary</td>
							<td>
								Our hosting and content delivery provider. It may set cookies to protect the site against automated
								traffic and to balance load.
							</td>
							<td>See Cloudflare's list</td>
							<td>See Cloudflare's list</td>
							<td>
								<a
									href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/"
									>Cloudflare cookies</a
								>
							</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>

			<p>You may find below the additional information and resources regarding the above mentioned services.</p>

			<ul>
				<li>
					Google Analytics - See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies"
						>Google Analytics privacy page</a
					> for more details.
				</li>
				<li>
					Google Programmable Search Engine - See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies"
						>Google privacy page</a
					> for more details.
				</li>
				<li>
					Cloudflare - See <a
						href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/"
						>Cloudflare documentation page</a
					> for more details.
				</li>
				<li>
					FirstPromoter - See <a href="https://firstpromoter.com/">FirstPromoter's privacy policy</a> for more details.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	@use '../../styles/variables' as *;

	.cookie-policy-page {
		min-height: 100vh;
		// The page surface stays light inside the theme-aware BaseLayout, so
		// re-emit the light token palette (the same convention as LegalLayout and
		// the forced-light header) and let the rules below read the tokens —
		// otherwise theme-aware inks like _base.scss's heading colour go
		// near-white in dark mode and vanish on this white surface.
		color-scheme: light;
		@include light-theme-tokens;
		background-color: var(--color-bg-surface);
	}

	.cookie-policy-content {
		max-width: 860px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		// Clear the fixed header ($header-height); the previous 60px let the H1
		// slide under it. The .tb-topbar sticky unit overlaps content by design, so
		// BaseLayout pages self-offset by the header height (see pricing/index.astro).
		padding: calc(#{$header-height} + 40px) 24px 80px;
		color: var(--color-text);
		line-height: 1.7;
		font-size: 16px;
		text-align: justify;

		h1 {
			font-size: 32px;
			font-weight: 600;
			margin-bottom: 8px;
		}

		.updated {
			@include text-s;
			color: var(--color-text-secondary);
			margin-bottom: 24px;
		}

		h3 {
			font-size: 20px;
			font-weight: 600;
			margin: 32px 0 8px;

			&::before {
				display: none;
			}
		}

		p {
			margin: 0 0 12px;
		}

		ul {
			margin: 0 0 12px;
			padding-left: 24px;
			list-style: disc;

			li {
				margin-bottom: 4px;
				list-style: disc;
				color: #75767c;
				font-size: 1.125rem;
				line-height: 1.6;

				&::marker {
					color: #75767c;
				}
			}
		}

		a,
		.cookie-settings {
			color: var(--color-primary);
			text-decoration: none;

			&:hover {
				text-decoration: underline;
			}
		}

		.cookie-settings {
			padding: 0;
			font: inherit;
			background: none;
			border: 0;
			cursor: pointer;
		}

		// Wide table: scrolls sideways on phones instead of widening the page.
		.cookie-table-wrap {
			overflow-x: auto;
			margin: 0 0 16px;
		}

		.cookie-table {
			@include text-s;
			width: 100%;
			border-collapse: collapse;
			text-align: left;

			th,
			td {
				border: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);
				padding: 8px 10px;
				vertical-align: top;
			}

			th {
				background: var(--color-bg-light);
				font-weight: 600;
			}
		}

		code {
			background: #f4f4f4;
			padding: 2px 6px;
			border-radius: 4px;
			font-size: 14px;
		}
	}
</style>
